  "description": "CEYCAN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H90 Cl2 Gd5 Mn2 N4 O34 3+,2(C1 H4 O1),3(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.593-4.356 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.32-131.81°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd5Mn2(LOMe)2(OH)4(Ac)6(MeOH)10Cl2]Cl3·2MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
